## 6. Summary

| Concept | Key Takeaway |
|---|---|
| Functional symbol table | Never mutates; creates new tables; uses BSTs for efficiency |
| Imperative symbol table | Mutates in place; uses hash tables; undo stack for scope exit |
| Hash table with chaining | O(1) insert/lookup; insert at head for shadowing; pop head for undo |
| Symbol interning | Converts strings to unique pointers for fast comparison |
| Scope management | Marksym or auxiliary stack to track scope boundaries |
| Multiple environments | Each module/class has its own table; combined for package scope |
| Forward references | Enabled by combining all class tables into a single environment |
